  "feel": "straight",
  "confidence": "high",
  "notes": "Mono-thematic: one 4-bar marcato theme restated louder, higher and faster. theme is the B minor statement the piece opens with (bars 1-8): a rising 1-2-3-4-5 run answered by a chromatic sidestep that spells C# major then C major, then the same run reaching up to the octave and a falling D major arpeggio. The deg 7 in that arpeggio is A NATURAL, not a leading tone -- it is the fifth of the D major chord, so it must not be raised to A#. theme-dominant is the second statement (bars 9-16), which Grieg transposes up a perfect fifth into F# major with a flattened sixth -- that is why its 6th and 7th degrees carry acc 1 (G# and A#) while the D natural stays diatonic. The crescendo is carried by the form energies rather than by new material. Harmony is a bar-granular reduction: the theme's second bar really changes chord mid-bar (C# major to C major), and v1 chords move only on barlines, so that bar carries the dominant it sits inside.",
